  "id": "Compound::DB01013 - Gene::2908",
  "verbalization": "Clobetasol Propionate, a therapeutic glucocorticoid, is implicated in multiple dermatological conditions through its interaction with Desoximetasone, a related steroid. The evidence suggests that Clobetasol Propionate may act via a shared mechanism with Desoximetasone, both of which bind to Nr3c1, a gene encoding the glucocorticoid receptor. This binding is a critical step in the signaling pathway that regulates inflammatory responses and skin homeostasis. The presence of a common lowest common ancestor between Clobetasol Propionate and Desoximetasone, both classified under the broader category of 3-Oxo-Delta(1),Delta(4)-Steroid, supports a shared biochemical pathway. The observed relationship between Clobetasol Propionate and Nr3c1 is thus likely mediated through the glucocorticoid receptor, with the therapeutic effects of Clobetasol Propionate potentially being modulated by its interaction with Nr3c1. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, though the exact role of Nr3c1 in the pathophysiology of the conditions it influences remains to be fully elucidated.",
